    "description": "Natural Petrified Wood Slab Tray\nFossilized Wood Footed Trivet / Display Plaque\nNatural History Specimen, Mid to Late 20th Century\nThis substantial petrified wood slab is cut from an authentic fossilized tree round, showcasing a mirror-polished top surface that reveals intricate concentric growth rings and vivid mineral crystallization. The stone exhibits a rich spectrum of natural tones including deep brick red, warm amber, ochre yellow, and smoky charcoal. The natural outer circumference retains its rough, textured bark-like matrix, while the underside is fitted with four applied pedestal feet for elevated tabletop use as a decorative tray, trivet, or mineral display.\nAuthentic petrified wood slab with high-gloss polished upper surface\nNatural rugged chert/bark perimeter displaying organic texture and matrix\nUnderside fitted with four molded feet for stable tabletop elevation\nMeasures approximately 9 inches long by 8 inches wide by 2 inches high; weighs 7.6 lbs\nCondition:\nVery good vintage condition. The polished surface displays bright luster with natural geological fractures, pit lines, and crystalline seams characteristic of ancient mineralized wood. Natural rough variation and earthy texture along the unpolished outer edge. Feet are securely attached to the underside with minor age-appropriate scuffing.",
